ce Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code module pure elemental subroutine calc_gamma_iapws06 ( self , T_in , P_in , coef ) implicit none class ( type_iapws06 ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( real64 ), intent ( in ) :: T_in ! [K] real ( real64 ), intent ( in ) :: P_in ! [Pa] type ( type_iapws_gibbs_coefficient ), intent ( inout ) :: coef real ( real64 ) :: tau , pi ! IAPWS-06 uses tau = T / Tt (Direct ratio, unlike IAPWS-97) tau = T_in / self % T_star ! pi = P / Pt pi = P_in / self % p_star call coef % reset () ! Calculate properties and store in coef ! These functions return Dimensional values (J/kg, m3/kg, etc.) coef % g = calc_gamma_iapws06_Ih ( self , tau , pi ) coef % g_p = calc_gamma_p_iapws06_Ih ( self , tau , pi ) coef % g_t = calc_gamma_t_iapws06_Ih ( self , tau , pi ) coef % g_pp = calc_gamma_pp_iapws06_Ih ( self , tau , pi ) coef % g_tt = calc_gamma_tt_iapws06_Ih ( self , tau , pi ) coef % g_pt = calc_gamma_tp_iapws06_Ih ( self , tau , pi ) end subroutine calc_gamma_iapws06","tags":"","url":"proc/calc_gamma_iapws06.html"},{"title":"initialize_type_iapws06 – IAPWS","text":"pure elemental module subroutine initialize_type_iapws06(self) Interface → Initialize the IAPWS-06 object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_iapws06 ), intent(inout) :: self Called by proc~~initialize_type_iapws06~~CalledByGraph proc~initialize_type_iapws06 initialize_type_iapws06 interface~initialize_type_iapws06 type_iapws06%initialize_type_iapws06 interface~initialize_type_iapws06->proc~initialize_type_iapws06 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code module pure elemental subroutine initialize_type_iapws06 ( self ) implicit none class ( type_iapws06 ), intent ( inout ) :: self self % T_star = 27 3.16d0 ! [K] Triple point temperature self % p_star = p_starIh ! [Pa] Triple point pressure ! Reference dimensionless pressure pi_0 corresponding to P = 101325 Pa self % pi_0 = 10132 5.0d0 / self % p_star self % R = 46 1.526d0 ! [J/kgK] end subroutine initialize_type_iapws06","tags":"","url":"proc/initialize_type_iapws06.html"},{"title":"calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 – IAPWS","text":"pure elemental module subroutine calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5(self, T_in, p_in, dcp_dT, dcp_dp) Interface → Analytic cp derivatives, evaluated only when requested. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_iapws97_region5 ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: T_in real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: p_in real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: dcp_dT real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: dcp_dp Called by proc~~calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5~~CalledByGraph proc~calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 interface~calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 type_iapws97_region5%calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 interface~calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5->proc~calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code module pure elemental subroutine calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5 ( self , T_in , p_in , dcp_dT , dcp_dp ) implicit none class ( type_iapws97_region5 ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( real64 ), intent ( in ) :: T_in , p_in real ( real64 ), intent ( out ) :: dcp_dT , dcp_dp real ( real64 ) :: tau , pi , y , jval , term , gtt , gttt , gttp real ( real64 ) :: xp ( 0 : 3 ), yp ( 0 : 9 ), t0p ( - 6 : 2 ) integer :: k , n , iexp , jexp tau = self % T_star / T_in pi = p_in / self % p_star y = tau xp ( 0 ) = 1.d0 do k = 1 , 3 xp ( k ) = xp ( k - 1 ) * pi end do yp ( 0 ) = 1.d0 do k = 1 , 9 yp ( k ) = yp ( k - 1 ) * y end do t0p ( 0 ) = 1.d0 do k = 1 , 2 t0p ( k ) = t0p ( k - 1 ) * tau end do do k = - 1 , - 6 , - 1 t0p ( k ) = t0p ( k + 1 ) / tau end do gtt = 0.d0 gttt = 0.d0 gttp = 0.d0 do n = 1 , N05_terms jexp = J0_r5 ( n ) if ( jexp == 0 . or . jexp == 1 ) cycle jval = real ( jexp , real64 ) term = n0_r5 ( n ) * jval * ( jval - 1.d0 ) gtt = gtt + term * t0p ( jexp - 2 ) if ( jexp /= 2 ) gttt = gttt + term * ( jval - 2.d0 ) * t0p ( jexp - 3 ) end do do n = 1 , Nr5_terms iexp = Ir_r5 ( n ) jexp = Jr_r5 ( n ) if ( jexp < 2 ) cycle jval = real ( jexp , real64 ) term = nr_r5 ( n ) * jval * ( jval - 1.d0 ) gtt = gtt + term * xp ( iexp ) * yp ( jexp - 2 ) if ( jexp > 2 ) gttt = gttt + term * ( jval - 2.d0 ) * xp ( iexp ) * yp ( jexp - 3 ) gttp = gttp + term * real ( iexp , real64 ) * xp ( iexp - 1 ) * yp ( jexp - 2 ) end do ! The ideal log(pi) term has no temperature derivatives. dcp_dT = self % R * tau ** 2 / T_in * ( 2.d0 * gtt + tau * gttt ) dcp_dp = - self % R * tau ** 2 / self % p_star * gttp end subroutine calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5","tags":"","url":"proc/calc_cp_derivatives_iapws97_region5.html"},{"title":"calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5 – IAPWS","text":"pure recursive module subroutine calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5(self, T_in, P_in, coef) Interface → Uses module_iapws_batch proc~~calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5~~UsesGraph proc~calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5 calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5 module~module_iapws_batch module_iapws_batch proc~calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5->module~module_iapws_batch ieee_arithmetic ieee_arithmetic module~module_iapws_batch->ieee_arithmetic iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~module_iapws_batch->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( type_iapws97_region5 ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: T_in (:) real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: P_in (:) real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: coef (:,:) Calls proc~~calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5~~CallsGraph proc~calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5 calc_gamma_batch_iapws97_region5 interface~calc_gamma_iapws97_region5 type_iapws97_region5%calc_gamma_iapws97_region5 proc~calc_gamma_batc